For keyboard controls, you do **not** need different event names for each arrow. Use one `"keydown"` event and check the value of `event.key`.

The arrow key names are:

```js
"ArrowUp"
"ArrowDown"
"ArrowLeft"
"ArrowRight"
```

For example:

```js
document.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
    if (event.key === "ArrowUp") {
        // move up
    } else if (event.key === "ArrowDown") {
        // move down
    } else if (event.key === "ArrowLeft") {
        // move left
    } else if (event.key === "ArrowRight") {
        // move right
    }
});
```

The event itself is `"keydown"`. The individual arrow names are values of `event.key`.

Other common keyboard events are:

- `"keydown"` — when a key is pressed
- `"keyup"` — when a key is released
- `"keypress"` — older event; avoid using it for this assignment

Use `"keydown"` for the Snake controls.

