    if (gameOver) {
        return;
    }

    direction = nextDirection;
    canTurn = true;

    const oldHead = snake[0];

    const newHead = {
        x: oldHead.x + direction.x,
        y: oldHead.y + direction.y
    };

    // Continue with the rest of your existing code...
};
```

### 3. Update `changeDirection`

Replace your current function with:

```js
const changeDirection = (newDirection) => {
    if (!canTurn) {
        return;
    }

    if (
        direction.x + newDirection.x === 0 &&
        direction.y + newDirection.y === 0
    ) {
        return;
    }

    nextDirection = newDirection;
    canTurn = false;
};
```

The important difference is that `direction` changes only inside `moveSnake`, once every 200 milliseconds. Fast key presses cannot create multiple turns during the same movement interval.

For example, while moving right:

- Press Up → accepted.
- Press Left immediately afterward → ignored because one turn has already been used.
- On the next movement, Up becomes the active direction.

Test the four cases:

- Right → Up → Left quickly
- Right → Down → Right quickly
- Up → Left → Down quickly
- Down → Right → Up quickly

The snake should make at most one turn per movement step.

